 "title": "Trust between Isaac, Abraham and the servant Eliezer",
 "summary": "Four colour-coded statements: Isaac trusts his father enough to be tied up for sacrifice; Abraham trusts his servant Eliezer, his sole heir; Isaac trusts Abraham and the most trusted servant to find him a bride; and the nameless servant points to Isaac, the Son.",
 "text": [
  {
   "lang": "en",
   "role": "body",
   "text": "Isaac trusts his father"
  },
  {
   "lang": "en",
   "role": "body",
   "text": "by allowing himself to be tied up to be sacrificed."
  },
  {
   "lang": "en",
   "role": "body",
   "text": "Abraham trusts his servant, Eliezer"
  },
  {
   "lang": "en",
   "role": "body",
   "text": "so much he was his sole heir."
  },
  {
   "lang": "en",
   "role": "body",
   "text": "Isaac trusts Abraham and most trusted servant"
  },
  {
   "lang": "en",
   "role": "body",
   "text": "to find a bride for him."
  },
  {
   "lang": "en",
   "role": "body",
   "text": "The most trusted servant"
  },
  {
   "lang": "en",
   "role": "body",
   "text": "remaining nameless, points to Isaac, the Son."
  }
